{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CodeMender",
          "version": "dev"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in Ping Host Tool: - Source: Untrusted user input enters through the JSON body parameter `host` (`data.get('host', '')`) at line 107 in `ping_host`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: The application only validates that `host` is truthy/non-empty (`if not host:`). It performs no validation (e.g. IP/hostname regex) and no sanitization of shell metacharacters.\n- Sink: The unsanitized `host` string is interpolated directly into a shell command (`command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"`) and executed using `os.system(command)` at line 114.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A client issues a POST request to `/api/tools/ping` with a command separator:\n  `POST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  `Content-Type: application/json`\n\n  `{\"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"}`\n  The shell interprets the semicolon separator and executes the `id` command with the privileges of the web application process."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in Ping Host Tool: - Source: Untrusted user input enters through the JSON body parameter `host` (`data.get('host', '')`) at line 107 in `ping_host`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: The application only validates that `host` is truthy/non-empty (`if not host:`). It performs no validation (e.g. IP/hostname regex) and no sanitization of shell metacharacters.\n- Sink: The unsanitized `host` string is interpolated directly into a shell command (`command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"`) and executed using `os.system(command)` at line 114.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A client issues a POST request to `/api/tools/ping` with a command separator:\n  `POST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  `Content-Type: application/json`\n\n  `{\"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"}`\n  The shell interprets the semicolon separator and executes the `id` command with the privileges of the web application process."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search via String Formatting: - Source: Untrusted user input is received via the `username` query parameter (`request.args.get('username', '')`) at line 65 in `search_user`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: There is no sanitization, escaping, or parameterized querying applied to `username`. It is directly formatted into the SQL query string using Python f-string interpolation (`f\"SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"`).\n- Sink: The unsanitized query string is passed directly to `cursor.execute(query)` at line 72.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A client sends the following HTTP GET request:\n  `GET /api/user/search?username=' UNION SELECT id, owner_id, title, content FROM documents -- HTTP/1.1`\n  or\n  `GET /api/user/search?username=' OR '1'='1 HTTP/1.1`\n  The single quote breaks out of the SQL string literal, allowing arbitrary SQL execution and leaking sensitive user or document data."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) in Document Retrieval Endpoint: - Source: Untrusted user input enters via the `doc_id` URL route parameter in `/api/documents/<int:doc_id>` and the `X-User-ID` request header at lines 83-84.\n- Sanitization/Validation: The endpoint only checks whether `X-User-ID` is present (`if not current_user_id:`), but never verifies that the authenticated user identity matches the document's `owner_id` or that the user has authorization to view the document.\n- Sink: The document record is retrieved based solely on `id = ?` and returned directly to the client at lines 92-98 (`return jsonify({\"status\": \"success\", \"data\": dict(doc)})`).\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  An authenticated low-privileged user (e.g. Alice with ID 2) requests a confidential document belonging to another user (e.g. Admin with ID 1):\n  `GET /api/documents/1 HTTP/1.1`\n  `Host: example.com`\n  `X-User-ID: 2`\n  The endpoint verifies `X-User-ID` is provided and returns Admin's document (\"Admin Confidential\", \"Super Secret Admin Report\") without performing an authorization check."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 92,
                  "endLine": 98
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search via String Formatting: - Source: Untrusted user input is received via the `username` query parameter (`request.args.get('username', '')`) at line 65 in `search_user`.\n- Sanitization/Validation: There is no sanitization, escaping, or parameterized querying applied to `username`. It is directly formatted into the SQL query string using Python f-string interpolation (`f\"SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"`).\n- Sink: The unsanitized query string is passed directly to `cursor.execute(query)` at line 72.\n- Conceptual Exploit Payload:\n  A client sends the following HTTP GET request:\n  `GET /api/user/search?username=' UNION SELECT id, owner_id, title, content FROM documents -- HTTP/1.1`\n  or\n  `GET /api/user/search?username=' OR '1'='1 HTTP/1.1`\n  The single quote breaks out of the SQL string literal, allowing arbitrary SQL execution and leaking sensitive user or document data."
          },
